  "briefing": [
    "The Glenmorran Hotel, at the head of Glen Morran in the Highlands. Sunday 25 January 2026: Burns Night. You came up on Friday for the hotel’s famous Burns supper and a few days’ walking. Queen Victoria took tea here, The Grey Lady of Glenmorran was filmed in its Great Hall, and its bar keeps four hundred whiskies. Since half past nine last night, black ice has closed the pass, and the hotel is cut off.",
    "At the supper the film’s star, Dame Vivienne Lisle, 78, did something nobody expected. She took her famous black diamond, the Black Ice, out of its display case and fastened it round the neck of the head housekeeper, Halina Kowalczyk, ‘Mrs K’ to three generations of guests. ‘For twenty winters this woman has looked after me,’ she said. ‘It’s hers.’ Mrs K went up to turn down the first-floor beds, wearing it.",
    "At two minutes to midnight the lights went out: the storm, everyone said. You sat in the Great Hall with everyone else, in candlelight, while Dame Vivienne sang Burns. At 00:24 the night porter got the lights back. At 06:40 this morning, Mrs K’s daughter Kasia found her mother dead on the floor of the linen room. The Black Ice was gone.",
    "The police will come up the glen behind the gritters this afternoon. Until then nobody can leave, and whoever killed Mrs K is still in the hotel. Kasia has asked you to find out who it was before the police arrive and the guests scatter. ‘My mother noticed everything,’ she says. ‘Nobody ever noticed her.’",
    "Alasdair Munro, the owner, has given you the run of the hotel, and Dr Morven Shaw, a GP who was at the supper, has examined Mrs K. Everyone who was in the Glenmorran last night is still here."
  ],
